{
  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "recovery-steer-identity-multiplier-placebo",
    "parent": "recovery-selection-null-steer-control",
    "kind": "ablate",
    "title": "Identity-multiplier placebo at the recovery-selection site: separate code-path/throughput cost from actual reweighting",
    "description": "Keep the null-steer diff in spur/spur-core/src/simulator/core/scheduler.rs byte-for-byte (same predicate evaluation, same counter increments, same candidate walk, same draw sites) but clamp the applied multiplier to exactly 1.0, so the term is provably incapable of changing any candidate's rank. Gate on a single bool `faults.recovery_weight_placebo` (default false, one evaluated value true) so the placebo is an overlay inside the existing arm set, not a new arm. Readout: stratified AND pooled depth>=4/6/8, throughput (runs/s), per-arm run counts, and the term's evaluated/present/won/contested/flipped counters — `flipped` MUST be 0, which is the build-correctness check that the placebo is truly inert. Falsifier: if depth still shifts by the parent band (-0.02..-0.06) with flipped==0, the null-steer and parent regressions were evaluation artifacts (throughput-driven arm-mix drift under round_robin's fixed wall clock), and every single-term event-side A/B at this site — including the recovery-anchored-to-own-inflight-sends 'clean monotone regression' — is uninterpretable as evidence about VR races. If it reads flat within the measured null band (|primary| <= ~0.003), the ~2.5k contested flips in 8.4e8 decisions really are load-bearing and the site is depth-fragile.",
    "category": "scheduler",
    "buildsOn": [
      "recovery scheduling",
      "steer term evaluation",
      "steer_terms counters"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 4,
    "expectedCost": 1.5,
    "rationale": "The recorded observation for recovery-selection-null-steer-control ends with exactly this action item: 'stop reading single-term A/B deltas at the recovery-selection site as causal until the compiled-in-but-inert placebo comes back flat.' Two consecutive runs produced -0.03..-0.07 depth deltas from perturbations that touched ~3e-6 of decisions with zero measured/acted downstream effect, and pooled/stratified disagreed by ~1.5x at the deep end — the signature of arm-mix drift, not steering. This is the only cheap experiment that separates 'the site is fragile' from 'this evaluation cannot resolve any term at this site', and the second answer retroactively invalidates a family of closed verdicts. It does not itself lift a rung, so it is capped below a mechanism hypothesis.",
    "generalityArgument": "The placebo consults no protocol state and can change no scheduling decision; it measures a property of the evaluation (draw sites, per-term cost, arm mix under a fixed wall clock), not of VR, its messages or its labels. The gating bool is removed with the experiment.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-30T12:00:00.000Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "[unparked iteration 5366] Pre-registered next step now that the null-steer control did NOT come back flat (-0.0377 primary, -0.0397 throughput); the placebo is the only way to split code-path cost from reweighting and close the family; falsifier: placebo reproduces the same negative deltas, proving overhead not steering."
